From eef19d9bdff8699e99c99e1ab92f9a34023e21ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stoatium Build <stoatium@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 16:05:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] debrand: drop the Gifbox explainer and the gifbox.me upsells

The picker shipped upstream's marketing: a one-time "GIFs are now powered by
Gifbox" card linking to stoat.gg, and two "Upload to Gifbox" buttons pointing
at gifbox.me. None of that is true for a fork pointed at whatever GIF service
VITE_GIFBOX_URL names, and the AGPL licenses none of those marks.

Search, categories and sending are untouched; only the promotion and the
styles it needed are gone. The two thrown errors now say "GIF" rather than
naming the service.
